  "summary": "San Jose Police Chief Paul Joseph announced that an SJPD officer was fired after accessing Flock ALPR data on his personal phone and providing it to a domestic violence suspect who used it to locate a victim. The chief said policy has been changed to prevent access from personal devices, and the case was referred to the district attorney. Immigrant rights group SIREN called for the cameras to be turned off.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The officer accessed license plate reader data and provided that to a suspect in a domestic violence situation, which enabled that suspect to locate a victim",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "This is a betrayal of the public trust -- plain and simple",
      "paragraph_idx": 7
    },
    {
      "quote": "Mass surveillance is not public safety and these cameras are only creating new threats",
      "paragraph_idx": 17
    }
  ],
